<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Zhengtong Emperor</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1427–1464</span> · Also known as Emperor Yingzong of Ming, Tianshun Emperor, Zhu Qizhen</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Zhengtong Emperor, Zhu Qizhen, ruled Ming <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a> from 1435 to 1449 and again, as the Tianshun Emperor, from 1457 to 1464. Urged by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eunuch">eunuch</a> Wang Zhen, he led a campaign against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oirats">Oirats</a> in 1449 and was captured by Esen at the Tumu Fortress. Released in 1450, he was kept under house arrest by his brother, the Jingtai Emperor, until a palace coup restored him in 1457.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/zhengtong-emperor.jpg" alt="Zhengtong Emperor" width="320" height="428" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ming_Yingzong_(1).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
